  "methodology": "Each post-disposal dereference happens after two CDP forced-GC rounds separated by a browser task, before changing the retained handle. This accommodates delayed DOM wrapper cleanup without using a dereference that keeps the target alive between rounds. The probe weakly observes the actual root CRCElement and HTMLCanvasElement; the retain case keeps only the public Texture handle. WeakRef only distinguishes JavaScript reachability; it cannot prove native/GPU reclamation.",
